# Playnite themes (monorepo policy)

## Shape: every theme is standalone

- A theme is an add-on with **`"kind": "theme"`** in **`src/extensions.json`**, laid out like the plugins:
  - `src/themes/<Theme>/AGENTS.md` — the theme's notes (sources, which token plays each key, shell, components, deviations, what is unverified).
  - `src/themes/<Theme>/info/` — `theme.yaml`, `InstallerManifest.yaml`, `danitesler_<key>.yaml`, `icon.png`, `LICENSE-*.txt` for everything bundled (Playnite's Default theme, icon sets).
  - `src/themes/<Theme>/src/` — the XAML the theme ships, at Playnite's Default-theme paths, plus `tokens.css` and `Constants.template.xaml`.
- Profile fields: **`themeSource`** (`src/themes/<Theme>/src`), `extensionManifest` (`info/theme.yaml`), `outputPath` (`artifacts/builds/themes/<key>`), `requiredApiVersion` = the **theme API** version. Packages are **`.pthm`**; database `Type` is **`ThemeDesktop`** / **`ThemeFullscreen`**.
- **No shared kits, no inheritance between themes.** A theme never reads another theme's files; nothing is copied in at build time except its own `src/` and `info/LICENSE*.txt`. The only thing themes share is the **key vocabulary** below. Other themes are a reference for *Playnite mechanics* and *which key a role uses*, never a source of styles or values.
- Build output is generated: `src/` copied, `Constants.xaml` rendered from `Constants.template.xaml` + `tokens.css`, `thememodifier.yaml`, licenses and `theme.yaml` added. Edit sources, never **`artifacts/builds/`**.

## One vocabulary, each theme's own design

- **Tokens keep the design system's names; keys don't.** `tokens.css` holds the system's tokens verbatim (the source of every value). XAML keys are the same in every theme: **Playnite's own keys** (`scripts/data/playnite-theme-api.json`) plus the **shared keys** in **`scripts/data/theme-keys.json`**. The template maps each key to the token that plays its role, so design-system names appear only in `tokens.css` and in template placeholders:

```xml
<!-- ❌ BAD: design-system key names -->
<SolidColorBrush x:Key="PrimerBgColorDefaultBrush" Color="{{bgColor-default}}" />
<Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource PrimerBgColorDefaultBrush}" />

<!-- ✅ GOOD: shared key, Primer token as its value -->
<SolidColorBrush x:Key="InputBackgroundBrush" Color="{{bgColor-default}}" />
<Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource InputBackgroundBrush}" />
```

- **Picking the key for a spot** (a color in a control template), in order:
  1. **Playnite palette key** when its role covers the spot and the design uses that key's token there. Playnite's Default files define the roles: `TextBrush` / `TextBrushDarker` text, `TextBrushDark` text on accent, `GlyphBrush` accent, `HoverBrush` hover, `ButtonBackgroundBrush` button fill, `NormalBorderBrush` control edge, `CheckBoxCheckMarkBkBrush`, `PopupBackgroundBrush` / `PopupBorderBrush`, `TooltipBackgroundBrush`, `ExpanderBackgroundBrush` cards, `WindowBackgourndBrush`, `WindowPanelSeparatorBrush` dividers, `WarningBrush`. If the design's value for such a role differs from what the palette key holds, point the palette key at the design's token (unrestyled views read it too; note it in the theme's AGENTS.md).
  2. **Shared general role** from `theme-keys.json`: `SelectedBrush`, `FocusBrush`, `FocusHaloBrush`, `DangerBrush`, `InputBackgroundBrush`, `PrimaryButton*`, `ShellBackgroundBrush`, ...
  3. **Shared control slot** (`<Control>[<State>]<Part>Brush`, e.g. `SliderTrackBrush`, `TopPanelItemCheckedBackgroundBrush`) only where the design gives that part its own token.
  4. When a design uses two values for one role in different controls, the main control takes the role's key and the other reuses the key of the token it shares (Primer's pressed `Button` uses `HoverBrush`; its pressed `RepeatButton` uses `ButtonPressedBackgroundBrush`).
  5. A role that is not in the vocabulary: add it to `theme-keys.json` first (key, type, group, one-line description), then use it. Never invent a key inside a theme.
- **Naming** (for new vocabulary entries): `<Control>[<Variant>][<State>]<Part><Type>` with Playnite's control names and spelling (`Button`, `ToggleButton`, `ComboBox`, `ListBox`, `GroupBox`, `SidebarItem`, `TopPanel`, `Tooltip`), never a design system's component names (ActionList, Card, AppBar, MenuPopover). General roles drop the control (`SelectedBrush`, `FocusBrush`); a plain fill drops the part (`SliderTrackBrush`, `MenuSeparatorBrush`). Spacing `<Control>Padding`; radii `ControlCornerRadius` (Playnite's, the medium step) and `CornerRadiusSmall` / `Large` / `XLarge` / `Full`; icons `Icon<Role>` drawn by `IconTemplate`; styles by what they style (`FocusVisual`, `BareTextBox`, `MainWindowButton`, `MainMenuButton`, `TopPanelSearchBox`, `SliderThumb`, `ScrollBarThumb`).
- **Each theme keeps its own design.** Values, radii, spacing, shell, icon set and component shapes come from its design system's published spec, pinned to a version in its `AGENTS.md`; only names are shared. Map by role, not by color (one source color can be several roles). Write the component spec in each file's header comment (component name, tokens, sizes). A design system is more than colors: its spacing (`Common.xaml`), its shell, its icons (`Media.xaml`) and its component shapes. Where WPF or Playnite can't follow the spec, list it under "Deviations" in `AGENTS.md`.

## ThemeModifier

ThemeModifier (Lacro59's add-on) recolors a theme by **replacing Playnite's palette brushes** (`TextBrush`, `GlyphBrush`, `HoverBrush`, `ButtonBackgroundBrush`, `PopupBackgroundBrush`, ... 24 in all) in the application resources, and edits a theme's own constants listed in `thememodifier.yaml`.

- Only `{DynamicResource <Brush>}` references follow a replaced brush. A `*Color` key, or a second key holding the same color, does not. So theme XAML reads **brushes only**; the build fails on a `Color` reference outside `Constants.xaml`. For a gradient, fill with the brush and put the gradient in an `OpacityMask` (see any theme's indeterminate `ProgressBar`).
- One sanctioned exception: `HtmlTextView.HtmlForeground` and `LinkForeground` (the game description) are Color-typed properties with a black default, so they read `TextColor` / `GlyphColor`; the build check allows exactly those two attributes, and ThemeModifier brush edits do not reach that text.
- Define palette and shared brushes as plain `SolidColorBrush` entries in the template. A brush that points at another brush can't follow an edit.
- `build-theme.ps1` generates **`thememodifier.yaml`** next to `theme.yaml`: every shared brush the theme defines (plus sized doubles such as `IconSize`), grouped and labelled from `theme-keys.json`, so every theme offers the same Edit constants list. Palette brushes listed in `playnitePaletteConstants` (the window background, `WindowBackgourndBrush`) lead their group there too, so the theme's own options can change them. Don't hand-edit it; change descriptions in `theme-keys.json`.

## How Playnite loads a theme (drives the hard rules)

Source: `source/Playnite/Themes.cs` (`ThemeManager.ApplyTheme`).

1. Only XAML whose relative path matches a file in Playnite's **Default** theme is loaded (`scripts/data/playnite-theme-api.json`); anything else is ignored.
2. Each theme file is first parsed **on its own**, with only Default resources present.
3. Files then merge in pairs, `Default/A.xaml` then `Theme/A.xaml`, in API order: `Constants.xaml`, `Common.xaml`, `Media.xaml`, `DefaultControls/*`, `CustomControls/*`, `DerivedStyles/*`, `Views/*`. The later definition of a key wins.
4. `Toolbox pack` skips any `Fonts/` folder and any file identical to the Default copy.

## Hard rules (Playnite fails silently otherwise)

- Theme files are **overlays**: only restyled keys. Keep every `PART_*` and every part Playnite code dereferences (`SearchBox` needs all of `PART_SeachIcon`, `PART_TextInpuText`, `PART_ClearTextIcon`). Start from the Default file at the snapshot's Playnite tag; change visuals and layout, not behavior.
- Theme keys via **`DynamicResource`**. **`StaticResource`** only for Playnite keys or keys defined earlier in the same file.
- `StaticResource {x:Type ContextMenu}` in a later file resolves to the theme's own style (files merge one by one). Use `BasedOn` that way instead of copying templates (SliderEx, GameMenu, GameGroupMenu, TrayContextMenu, TopPanelMenu).
- When a Default style references a sibling in its own file with `StaticResource`, redefine both (`Separator` + `MenuItem.SeparatorStyleKey`).
- `BaseStyle` already sets Opacity 0.5 when disabled; styles based on it must not add their own `IsEnabled` opacity trigger (0.25).
- Focus: buttons, toggles, checkboxes, tabs use a keyed `FocusVisualStyle` (`FocusVisual`; keyboard only). Text inputs draw focus on `IsKeyboardFocusWithin`. No `IsKeyboardFocused` border triggers on buttons (mouse clicks give keyboard focus too).
- No hard-coded colors in theme XAML: add a token, a template line, and a vocabulary entry if the role is new.
- Icon resources Playnite copies (`Media.xaml` menu icons such as `AddGameIcon`, `PlayIcon`) are rebuilt from a `TextBlock`'s glyph and font, so a vector there is lost. To use the design system's icons, make each key a `sys:String` theme-relative PNG path (Playnite loads it through `ThemeFile`), rendered with `scripts/render-icons.ps1` from the theme's `icons.json`. Vector icons elsewhere are `Icon<Role>` geometries drawn through `IconTemplate`.
- Game overview (`Views/DetailsViewGameOverview.xaml`, `Views/GridViewGameOverview.xaml`): each theme lays it out its own way. Every `PART_*` is optional (Playnite null-checks each one), but a name may appear once. Values in lists (`PART_Items*`) are Buttons Playnite styles with `{StaticResource PropertyItemButton}` from code, so the only styling hook is the theme's `DerivedStyles/PropertyItemButton.xaml`; it switches look on the owning list's `Tag` (`Chip`) through a `RelativeSource AncestorType=ItemsControl` DataTrigger. `HtmlTextView` is a `StackPanel` (no `Foreground`) and takes `Color`s: set `TextElement.Foreground` and `Tag` to brushes and bind `HtmlForeground` / `LinkForeground` to `(TextElement.Foreground).Color` / `Tag.Color`.
- Game overview metadata pane: **every** field of Playnite's "Game fields to be displayed on details panel" list lives in ONE pane (the right column of the details page, the Game details area of the grid panel), never split between a header, stat cards or chips elsewhere. Six groups in this order, each field a container `x:Name="PART_Elem<Field>"` (Playnite toggles its `Visibility`) plus a label (`LOC` key) and the value part: **progress** (CompletionStatus, PlayTime, LastPlayed, RecentActivity, Added), **scores** (Community, Critic, User; `TextBlockGameScore`), **about** (Developers, Publishers, ReleaseDate, Series, AgeRating, Region), **tags** (Platform, Genres, Categories, Features, Tags; `Tag="Chip"` `WrapPanel`), **library** (Library, Source, Version, InstallSize, InstallDirectory), **links**. Each group is a `Border` that collapses through a `MultiDataTrigger` on `{Binding Visibility, ElementName=PART_Elem<Field>}` = `Collapsed` (a `DataTrigger` for one field), so a game with few fields shows few groups and no stray separator. Separator between groups: a 1px top border on the group (margin above, padding below) inside a `ClipToBounds` wrapper whose inner panel has negative top and bottom margins, so the first group draws no rule; or plain space where the design system has no rules. Labels are existing Playnite `LOC` keys (`LOCTimePlayed`, `LOCDevelopersLabel`, `LOCGenresLabel`, ...) with no group captions, because a theme cannot ship a `Localization` folder. Wide details pane: caption column beside the value; narrow grid panel: caption above the value. Do not use `GridEx` for it: `AutoLayoutColumns` would put hidden rows back in the flow.
- Slider: set `Track.Thumb` last (Track stacks parts in the order set). `ScrollContentPresenter` clips, so anything drawn outside an item needs the gutter as the panel's margin.
- No `DropShadowEffect` on popups or tiles; popups keep a 1px edge (WPF popups are layered windows). Wrap masked art (`OpacityMask`) in an element with `BitmapCache`.
- No `--` inside XML comments, no `{{` / `}}` in template comments, no **`Fonts/`** folder.
- Keep **`ThemeApiVersion`** as low as the theme allows (2.9.0 = Playnite 10.45+). Major must match Playnite's.

## Template placeholders (`Constants.template.xaml`)

| Placeholder | Result |
|-------------|--------|
| `{{name}}` | token color, alpha kept |
| `{{name@surface}}` / `{{name@surface@base}}` | flattened onto the surface (use for popup edges); a translucent last surface is an error |
| `{{name/NN}}` | token at NN% opacity |
| `{{a?b}}` | first token that exists |
| `{{name\|#hex}}` | fallback literal |
| `{{px:name[\|fallback]}}` | length in px (rem, px, var(), calc()) |
| `{{text:name\|fallback}}` | raw text (font names) |
| `{{TODO}}` | fails the build with "not mapped yet" |

Tokens are read from `:root` / `@theme`, and selectors containing `dark` override them. Errors report file, line and key.

## Build checks

`build-theme.ps1` (and `validate-extension.ps1`) fail on: files outside Playnite's list, unrendered placeholders, malformed XML, unknown references, cross-file `StaticResource`, keys that are neither Playnite's nor in `theme-keys.json`, a vocabulary key with the wrong type, `Color` references outside `Constants.xaml`, a `Fonts/` folder. Missing **required** vocabulary keys are a warning in `build-theme.ps1` (a theme in progress still deploys) and an error in `validate-extension.ps1`.

## Commands

- New theme: **`.\scripts\new-theme.ps1 -Name "My Theme" -Key mytheme [-DesignSystem "My DS"] [-TokensCss <file>]`**
- Build + checks: **`.\scripts\build-theme.ps1 -Extension <key> [-Deploy] [-DeployPath <Themes folder>]`** (also via `build-plugin.ps1`)
- Validate / package: `validate-extension.ps1`, `build-artifacts.ps1 -VerifyInstaller` (branch on `kind`).
- New Playnite release: **`.\scripts\update-playnite-theme-api.ps1 -PlayniteSource <checkout> -PlayniteVersion <tag>`**, then diff the Default theme for every file each theme ships.

## Versioning and releases

Same policy as plugins (**`playnite-extension-versioning.mdc`**, **`playnite-github-releases-per-extension.mdc`**): bump **`theme.yaml`** `Version` + **`InstallerManifest.yaml`** only when cutting a release; tag **`{key}-v{version}`**; one GitHub Release per theme with its **`.pthm`**.

